# Runtime data — the whole directory: it holds the SQLite database plus
# session_secret.txt / proxy_token.txt, which the *.db globs below do not cover.
/data/

*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.log

# rules.md was here. It is tracked now, deliberately: it is the build/review
# runbook, and the §14 machinery in it (the two-pass suite split, the transport
# probe) is real work that existed on exactly one machine. Checked before
# un-ignoring -- it carries no credentials, and the two operational identifiers
# in it (this host's Tailscale name and the default SSH key path) are already
# in Caddyfile, tests/test_db.py and two design docs.

# Pedro's running request log + the hook/settings that populate it. Private,
# same reasoning as CLAUDE.md below: operational log of this deployment's
# owner, not something a reader of the source needs. (rules.md used to be
# named here too; it is tracked now -- see above.)
/PT_request.md
/.claude/settings.local.json
# Agent instructions for this checkout. Deliberately not published: it describes
# how turns reach the model backends on *this* deployment -- the proxy hop, the
# credential variables, the routing table -- which is operational detail about a
# running host rather than something a reader of the source needs.
/CLAUDE.md

# Pedro's own running log of requests made to this project and their outcomes.
# Personal/operational, not project documentation -- same reasoning as
# CLAUDE.md above.
/requests-log.md

# Security scan output
.gitleaks-report.json
trivy-results.sarif

# Editors and operating systems
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Throwaway diagnostics kept out of commits. scratch_qdiag.py answered "why do
# some chats show questions and others not"; its findings are now pinned by
# tests/test_qa_approval_questions.py and tests/test_qa_question_marker.py.
scratch_*.py
.worktrees/

# Throwaway visual-brainstorming mockups (screens + click events), distinct
# from .superpowers/sdd/ which IS tracked (spec-driven-development artefacts).
.superpowers/brainstorm/
